>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `remove_arith`, `remove_arith_split`

``` hol4
linarithData.remove_arith : string -> unit
linarithData.remove_arith_split : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Remove persistent linarith facts or operator-splitting rules.

Each function records and immediately applies a persistent `REMOVE` delta
for its corresponding theorem set. The removal is inherited by child
theories and remains effective when declarations are reloaded. Names may
use database form `Theory.name`; kernel form `Theory$name` is also
recognised. Removing an absent, valid name is harmless. The `[arith]` and
`[arith_split]` sets are independent.

### Failure

Fails if a supplied `Theory.name` database name cannot be parsed. A string
in `Theory$name` kernel form is used directly as a table key. Removing an
absent name does not fail.

### Example

The following declarations are removed from their separate sets in the
current theory.

``` hol4
Theorem temporary_arith_fact[arith]:
  (0 : num) <= 1
Proof
  simp []
QED

Theorem temporary_arith_split[arith_split]:
  !P b x y.
    P (if b then (x : num) else y) <=>
    (b ==> P x) /\ (~b ==> P y)
Proof
  rw []
QED

val linarith_doc_theory = Theory.current_theory ();

val _ =
  linarithData.remove_arith
    (linarith_doc_theory ^ ".temporary_arith_fact");

val _ =
  linarithData.remove_arith_split
    (linarith_doc_theory ^ ".temporary_arith_split");
```

